  "id": "COMPOUND:28769 - PROTEIN:366",
  "verbalization": "Ivalin Acetate is shown to interact with Tyrosine--tRNA ligase, mitochondrial, which is a target of multiple compounds, including Nortrilobolide and tanzawaic acid B. These compounds are all implicated in the regulation of Betaine--homocysteine S-methyltransferase 1, suggesting a potential pathway where Ivalin Acetate may exert its effects through a shared mechanism of action on this enzyme. The evidence indicates that Ivalin Acetate may inhibit Betaine--homocysteine S-methyltransferase 1, possibly by interfering with the activity of its target enzyme, Tyrosine--tRNA ligase, mitochondrial. This mechanism is supported by the presence of a direct interaction between Ivalin Acetate and the enzyme, as well as the involvement of multiple compounds with similar targets. The integration of these findings suggests that Ivalin Acetate may act as a competitive inhibitor of Betaine--homocysteine S-methyltransferase 1, potentially modulating its activity in cellular processes. The evidence is consistent with a mechanistic link between Ivalin Acetate and Betaine--homocysteine S-methyltransferase 1, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the exact mode of action and therapeutic potential.",
